-- title:
--   m-torsion of the inertia-generated subgroup of J₀(Mq')
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and $q'$ a prime not dividing $M$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q'$ in the sense of the project's predicate `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. the image of $q'$ lies in the nonunits of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A` and assume $\kappa$ has decidable equality, that the set `ssPlaces q' M` $\kappa$ is finite, and that $M q' \neq 0$. Here `ssPlaces q' M` $\kappa$ consists of those places $w$ of the function field `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa$ $M$ (the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by the two $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC`) which are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w(\,$`jGeomGen`$\,) \in$ `ssJSet q'` $\kappa$ — the supersingular $j$-invariants. Finally let $m$ be a positive integer coprime to $q'$. Consider the additive subgroup $\mathcal{T}_{\mathbb{Z}}$ of `JZero (M * q')` — the group of degree-zero divisor classes, i.e. degree-zero divisors modulo principal divisors, of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full modular function field of level $Mq'$ — generated by all elements of the form $\sigma \cdot x - x$, where $\sigma$ runs over `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ inside its decomposition subgroup) and $x$ runs over the classes killed by some positive integer coprime to $q'$. The theorem asserts two things: the subtype of elements $y \in \mathcal{T}_{\mathbb{Z}}$ with $m \cdot y = 0$ is finite, and its cardinality equals $m^{\#\,\mathrm{ssPlaces}(q', M, \kappa) - 1}$.
--
--   This is the toric-rank count for $J_0(Mq')$ at $q'$: the dual graph of the special fibre of $X_0(Mq')$ at $q'$ has two vertices joined by one edge for each supersingular point, so the toric part of the reduction has dimension one less than the number of supersingular places, and the inertia-generated subgroup of prime-to-$q'$ torsion sees exactly that torus. It is used in [`ModularCurve.toric_sp_surjective_of_jZeroSemistableSpecialization_ssPlaces`](thm.html#ModularCurve.toric_sp_surjective_of_jZeroSemistableSpecialization_ssPlaces), and rests on the cardinality computation [`AlgebraicCurve.GluedPic0.natCard_ker_toPic0Pair_inf_torsionBy`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.GluedPic0.natCard_ker_toPic0Pair_inf_torsionBy) for the glued degree-zero class group of a pair of curves identified along a finite set of rational places.
